      "side": 1,
      "message": "These functions seem like they should go in a private implementation header file, not the one we\u0027re going to expose to others for vendor hooking. Only `rust_binderfs.c` should be calling these functions (by referencing them through DEFINE_SHOW_ATTRIBUTE), not anyone who imports the global `rust_binder.h`. Since we\u0027re about to start explicitly opening that header up to vendors, I think it makes more sense to put the `fops` and all of these functions into a `drivers/android/binder/rust_binder.h` or `rust_binder_internal.h` file or similar. Such a header could then include the stanzas you plucked from `rust_internal.h`",
      "revId": "26d514fa8852d8f0f9ca74a146169b94cffe4600",
